<node id="claim_msi_stabilizes_ru">
  <data key="d28">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d29">Strong metal–support interaction provided by nickel–vanadium LDH stabilizes the reactive atomic Ru site, producing only a small fluctuation in Ru oxidation state toward cathodic HER without reconstruction.</data>
  <data key="d38">site_stabilization</data>
  <data key="d39">Strong metal–support interaction provided by nickel–vanadium LDH stabilizes the reactive atomic Ru site, producing only a small fluctuation in Ru oxidation state toward cathodic HER without reconstruction.</data>
  <data key="d40">mixed</data>
  <data key="d30">The abstract presents this as the role of the atomic metal–support interaction in maintaining the Ru site during HER.</data>
  <data key="d31">["claim_msi_stabilizes_ru"]</data>
  <data key="d32">1</data>
  <data key="d33">broad_mechanism_abstract</data>
  <data key="d34">broad_abstract_support</data>
  <data key="d35">True</data>
  <data key="d36">abstract</data>
  <data key="d37">type: MechanismClaim
