source depth: abstract
epistemic use: exploration/bridge; verify before target-domain premise use
description: The abstract presents this as the role of the atomic metal–support interaction in maintaining the Ru site during HER.</data>
</node>
<node id="claim_ru_stabilizes_ni">
  <data key="d28">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d29">The atomic Ru site stabilizes the Ni site, giving it greater structural tolerance toward bond constriction and structural distortion during Ni oxidation in anodic OER and promoting an increase in Ni oxidation state that contributes to OER performance.</data>
  <data key="d38">dual_site_bifunctionality</data>
  <data key="d39">The atomic Ru site stabilizes the Ni site, giving it greater structural tolerance toward bond constriction and structural distortion during Ni oxidation in anodic OER and promoting an increase in Ni oxidation state that contributes to OER performance.</data>
  <data key="d40">mixed</data>
  <data key="d30">The abstract assigns complementary stabilization and catalytic roles to Ru and Ni sites.</data>
  <data key="d31">["claim_ru_stabilizes_ni"]</data>
  <data key="d32">1</data>
  <data key="d33">broad_mechanism_abstract</data>
  <data key="d34">broad_abstract_support</data>
